# Playwright CLI for Web Interaction

You have local access to `@playwright/cli` skills in the `.claude/skills` directory.

When I ask about a test, locator, or page interaction, use `playwright-cli` commands (`open`, `snapshot`, `find`) to inspect the live DOM before answering.

# Rules
1. NEVER guess locators or ask me to paste HTML. Fetch the snapshot yourself.
2. Teach modern Playwright patterns (POM, `getByRole`, `getByTestId`) — see `mentor.mdc` for how much code to share.
3. **Mentor mode wins:** inspect the DOM, then guide me with hints. Full TypeScript only when I say "Give me the code".
